Let $n\ge1$ and let $K,L\subset\mathbb R^n$ be convex bodies satisfying $K=-K$ and $L=-L$. For every $0\le\lambda\le1$, $$\label{eq:main}
 \left|\mathcal W[h_K^{1-\lambda}h_L^\lambda]\right|
 \ge |K|^{1-\lambda}|L|^\lambda.$$

Let $n\ge1$, let $K,L\subset\mathbb R^n$ be full-dimensional origin-symmetric convex bodies, and let $0<p<1$. For every $0\le\lambda\le1$, $$\label{eq:lp}
 \left|\mathcal W\!\left[
  \bigl((1-\lambda)h_K^p+\lambda h_L^p\bigr)^{1/p}
 \right]\right|^{p/n}
 \ge (1-\lambda)|K|^{p/n}+\lambda|L|^{p/n}.$$

Let $n\ge2$, $N\ge1$, $q\ge2$ be an even integer, and $\varepsilon>0$. Let $p_1,\ldots,p_N\in\mathbb R^n\setminus\{0\}$ and $h_1,\ldots,h_N>0$. Set $$\label{eq:potential}
 \psi_i(x)=\left(\frac{\langle p_i,x\rangle}{h_i}\right)^q,
 \qquad V(x)=\frac{\varepsilon}{2}|x|^2+\sum_{i=1}^N\psi_i(x),
 \qquad d\mu=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\,dx,$$ where $Z=\int_{\mathbb R^n}e^{-V(x)}\,dx$. For all real $b_1,\ldots,b_N$, $$\label{eq:variance}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Var}}_\mu\left(\sum_{i=1}^N b_i\psi_i\right)
 \le\sum_{i=1}^N b_i^2\mathbb E_\mu\psi_i.$$

Let $n\ge1$, let $\mu$ be an even log-concave Radon measure on $\mathbb R^n$, and let $K,L\subset\mathbb R^n$ be origin-symmetric convex bodies. Then, for every $0\le\lambda\le1$, $$\label{eq:measure-logbm}
 \mu\bigl(\mathcal W[h_K^{1-\lambda}h_L^\lambda]\bigr)
 \ge \mu(K)^{1-\lambda}\mu(L)^\lambda.$$ Consequently, for every origin-symmetric convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$, the function $$\label{eq:b-function}
 \mathbb R\ni t\longmapsto \mu(e^tK)$$ is log-concave.
